# <%= projectName %>

<%= answers.description %>

A [Palantir PACK](https://github.com/palantir/pack) starter workspace made of three
packages that build on each other:

| Package | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `packages/schema` | The document schema (`@palantir/pack.schema`), plus scripts to build its IR and generate the SDK. |
| `packages/sdk` | The generated, typed SDK. **Generated from the schema** — see below. |
| `packages/app` | A minimal Vite + React app that wires up the PACK libraries and consumes the SDK. |

This workspace uses plain [npm workspaces](https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/using-npm/workspaces)
— there is no build orchestrator, so the steps below are coordinated manually.

## 1. Install

```bash
npm install
```

## 2. Generate the SDK from the schema

`packages/sdk` ships as a stub. Populate it from the schema before building or
running the app:

```bash
npm run sdk-gen
```

This compiles `packages/schema/src/schema.mjs` to an IR and runs the SDK generator,
writing the typed SDK into `packages/sdk/src`. Re-run it whenever you change the schema.

## 3. Build the SDK

```bash
npm run build:sdk
```

## 4. Deploy the document type

<% if (answers.firstParty) { -%>
This is a first-party pack (document type `<%= answers.documentTypeName %>`). Build the asset
to bundle with your application:

```bash
npm run build:asset
```

To iterate against a dev stack before the asset ships, deploy the document type directly
(set `FOUNDRY_URL`, `FOUNDRY_TOKEN`, and `ONTOLOGY_RID` first):

```bash
npm run deploy
```
<% } else { -%>
Deploy the document type defined in `packages/schema` to your Foundry stack. Deployment
authenticates with a Foundry token rather than the browser OAuth flow: generate one under
**User Settings → Tokens** in Foundry and export it as `FOUNDRY_TOKEN`. The stack URL and
Compass parent folder you supplied when scaffolding are already baked into the deploy
script, so that token is the only value you need to set:

```bash
export FOUNDRY_TOKEN=<your-token>
npm run deploy
```
<% } -%>

## 5. Run the app

`packages/app/.env.local` was pre-filled from the answers you gave when scaffolding.
Double-check the values (Foundry client id, API URL, and ontology RID) — see
`packages/app/.env.example` for the full list — then:

```bash
npm run dev
```

On first load the app kicks off the OAuth flow, redirecting you to Foundry to sign in and
then back to `/auth/callback`.

## Typical loop

Because there is no orchestrator, remember the dependency order whenever the schema
changes:

```
edit packages/schema/src/schema.mjs
  -> npm run sdk-gen      (regenerate packages/sdk)
  -> npm run build:sdk    (compile the SDK)
  -> npm run dev          (the app picks up the new types)
```
